<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Turov</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Turaw</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Turov is a small town on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pripyat-river">Pripyat River</a> in Gomel region, southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belarus">Belarus</a>, and one of the oldest towns in the country. First mentioned in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/primary-chronicle">Primary Chronicle</a> under the year 980, it was the seat of a principality of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kievan-rus">Kievan Rus'</a> and of a bishopric whose most famous <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> was the 12th-century preacher <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyril-of-turov">Cyril of Turov</a>. Excavations have uncovered the foundations of a 12th-century church.</p></div>
